<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77712" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰν-ώλεθρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄλεθρος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>utterly destroyed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐξαπόλλυται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.37
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θρως</span>
			, found also <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				3.16.2
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανωλέθρους τὸ πᾶν . . ὀλέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1009
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πεσεῖν, γενέσθαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				934
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				552
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλιν πανώλεθρον ἐκθαμνίσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					71
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένος π. ἀναστρέψαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1239
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ξυναρπάσαι τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					839
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in moral
			sense, <i>utterly abandoned</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς π. Ἀτρείδαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					322
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ π. μήτηρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					86
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτε σὺν πανωλέθροισιν οὔτ᾽ ἄνευ
					πανωλέθρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					1039
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>all-destructive, ruinous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. κακόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.85
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμβολαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					562
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					414
				</span></i>
			.</div>
